        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(voice-call): share webhook replay tracking",
        "body": "Supersedes #98712 because the contributor fork predates the current `main` history and cannot be refreshed through GitHub's verified branch-edit path without replaying unrelated repository history.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where mock-provider webhook verification did not supply a stable verified request key, so duplicate deliveries could repeat voice-call side effects.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwilio, Plivo, Telnyx, and Mock now use one bounded replay tracker instead of provider-local cache variants. Verified request identity stays provider-derived while replay lifetime and eviction remain consistent across carriers.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRepeated verified webhook deliveries are acknowledged without processing the same call event twice, including in mock-provider and test deployments.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused local voice-call suite: 71/71 tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox focused suite: 71/71 tests passed.\n- Real TCP server probe sent the same POST twice: both returned 200 while exactly one event was processed.\n- Maintainer rewrite removed 190 lines of duplicate provider-local replay logic while centralizing the bounded 10-minute behavior.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: clean, 0.97 confidence.\n- Original contributor credit from #98712 is preserved in the commit.\n\nKnown proof gaps: none for the replay/deduplication path.\n",
